msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:129
msgid "[Paste here. On the same card, press \"Test from the internet\", then copy the result.]"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:131
msgid "HOW TO READ THE DATA ABOVE"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:132
msgid "- The \"Server\" block lists the web server, PHP SAPI and PHP limits. Web server and SAPI together decide whether an Authorization header survives to PHP, which is the most common cause of \"it worked yesterday and now the token is rejected\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:133
msgid "- The \"Diagnostics\" block lists every check as ID, status and label. FAIL is a directly observed fault. WARN is a sign worth ruling out, not proof. UNKNOWN means the check could not run and proves nothing either way — do not treat it as a pass or a failure."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:134
msgid "- Some check details read \"[details withheld]\" because they can identify WordPress users or API tokens. Treat those as status-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:136
msgid "WHAT I NEED FROM YOU"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:137
msgid "1. Name the single most likely cause, based only on the data above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:138
msgid "2. Quote the exact line or lines from the data that support that conclusion."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:139
msgid "3. Give me step-by-step instructions to fix it on a WordPress site, in plain language."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:140
msgid "4. If the data is not enough to reach a conclusion, say exactly what is missing instead of guessing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:141
msgid "5. If a check you rely on is UNKNOWN, tell me how to make it answerable rather than working around it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:143
msgid "THINGS THAT ARE USUALLY THE CAUSE, SO CHECK THEM FIRST"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:144
msgid "- Permalinks set to \"Plain\": WordPress writes no rewrite rules, so /wp-json/ and /.well-known/ return 404 before PHP runs, and OAuth discovery fails even though the endpoint appears to work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:145
msgid "- The Authorization header never reaching PHP: on Apache the RewriteRule WordPress writes into .htaccess passes it, and under FastCGI or PHP-FPM CGIPassAuth On in the server configuration does too; nginx needs the equivalent fastcgi_param. From outside, a stripped header and a wrong token look like the same 401."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:146
msgid "- A site behind a proxy or CDN that terminates HTTPS: PHP then sees the request as insecure and every OAuth request is refused, while the site is perfectly secure for visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:147
msgid "- A security or firewall plugin, or a host-level rule, refusing the request before WordPress sees it. This is invisible from inside WordPress, which is what the external test is for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-support-text.php:148
msgid "- A token whose permissions, OAuth scope, or WordPress user role leave it able to see no tools at all."
msgstr ""

